# Hold mode latch and run continuation (mandatory — do not regress)

**Status:** User-confirmed fix v0.8.362 (2026-07-29). Full pattern: [AGENTS.md §8.20](../../AGENTS.md#820-hold-mode-latch-and-run-continuation-mandatory--do-not-regress). Mistake log: [§9.6](../../AGENTS.md#96-regression-mistake-log-오답노트--agents-only).

## Rule

| Use | API | Emits `hotkeyHoldEnded`? |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Loop / tap lane “still holding?” polls** | `HotkeyManager::isHoldBindingStillActiveForRun` | **Never** |
| **Periodic latch heal** (`reconcileHoldLatchForActiveHoldSessions`) | `reconcileHoldBindingDown` | Only via deferred KEYUP recheck (not one-shot `GetAsyncKeyState` miss) |

**Do not** call `reconcileHoldBindingDown` from `shouldContinueRunSession`, worker fast-repeat hold checks, `HoldKeyTapMultiplexer` `shouldContinue`, or `launchHoldKeyTapRun` — it used to emit hold-end on a single async key miss (especially same-key KeyPress Tap pulses).

## Manual verify

Hold Q/W/E/R (tap-only or full workflow) with game foreground: key stays down → repeats; release → stops. Q/W/E/R together without cross-killing sessions.
